Command:        CREDITS
Purpose:        Display your current file transfer credit standing
Available at:   All command prompts (>)

This command tells you everything you need to know about what you've uploaded, and how much you can download.  The following are displayed:

        Total uploads:     Everything that you've ever uploaded to the
                           system is included here.
        Total downloads:   Everything that you've ever downloaded from
                           the system is included here (including free
                           items, Yanks, and Gfile downloads).
        Default ratios:    Unless you have 'infinite' credit status,
                           everytime that you upload to the system,
                           credits are added to your credit balance.  These
                           ratios determine whether you get 1 credit for
                           one upload (1:1) or two for every upload (2:1),
                           etc.  This is called a 'default' because each
                           subboard may optionally be configured to use any
                           other ratio as the sysop determines.
        Total credits:     Credits you have that may be applied toward
                           future downloads.  These may have been accumulated
                           by past uploads, or may have been given 'free' to
                           you by the sysop.  These determine the EXACT
                           number of files and bytes that you may download,
                           unless a subboard is configured otherwise to
                           subtract any percentage of the actual credits.
        Usable today:      Because the system may have in effect restrictions
                           on how much you can download in any one day, the
                           number of usable credits may be lower than your
                           actual total credits.
